  "answer_markdown": "VoyageFlow recommends booking accommodations 3–6 months in advance for late‑March and early‑April cherry‑blossom travel [tokyo-spring-guide::001]. Flights from North America and Europe often sell out 2–3 months ahead for late‑March trips, so secure those early as well [tokyo-spring-guide::004]. Popular ryokan (traditional inns) should be booked 4–6 months in advance, and restaurant reservations at high‑demand venues should be made before you arrive [tokyo-spring-guide::004].",
